.Dd October 4, 2026
.Dt KNOWLEDGE-INFRASTRUCTURE 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm knowledge-infrastructure
.Nd knowledge infrastructure for LLMs
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Em Knowledge Infrastructure for LLMs
.Pp
Knowledge infrastructure for LLMs: a language model can only work from what
someone wrote down and put in front of it, and most companies that bought AI
maintain their code and little else.
.Pp
Canonical copy:
.Bl -item -compact -offset indent
.It
.Lk https://coetzeestefan.substack.com/p/knowledge-infrastructure-for-llms
.El
.Sh TERMS
Definitions in the wording of the published piece.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Knowledge infrastructure (for LLMs)
The written, indexed, checked and maintained knowledge a language model runs
on, plus the routines that keep it true.
.It Markovian memory
At runtime the next token depends only on what is in the context window, so
anything outside the window does not exist for it.
.It Entry point
The one file a model reads first in a domain, pointing to everything else.
.It Failure record
What went wrong, the fix and the preventing rule, loaded at the start of
every session.
.It Output boundary
The point where a model's output leaves the model and someone acts on it;
the place to put mechanical checks.
.It Wire format
A document written for a model to read first, as in Write for the Codec.
.It Nothing exists in a vacuum
Every behaviour a model shows was forced into existence by something, the
corpus, the training signal or the harness.
.El
